# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_EXIT
	bool "Rust process exit, reparenting and wait"
	depends on RUST
	default y
	help
	  Build all process-exit, process-reparenting, mm-owner replacement,
	  zombie-reaping, wait and waitid syscall algorithms from kernel/exit.rs
	  in the original exit.o slot. Configured layouts and constants come
	  from native headers. Native compiler, locking, architecture and
	  uaccess primitives plus syscall/initcall/export metadata live in
	  exit_helpers.o. Exit-owned data and initializers remain in Rust.
	  All original feature-dependent behavior is retained.

	  The unchanged exit.c is retained for deliberate original-C reference
	  configurations. Rust acceptance must verify CONFIG_RUST_EXIT=y and
	  reject a C exit.o provider before running the original C tests.
